{"description":"Sibling duo participants with an IT background and an interest in astronomy and space exploration. Creating an educational storytelling project about NASA’s abandoned equipment on the Moon and Mars.","image":null,"summary":"Space Explorers: Where Are They Now? is an interactive website where kids discover the stories of NASA's rovers, spacecraft and equipment across the Moon, Mars and deep space. Through mission stories, real NASA images, a map, a timeline and a quiz, visitors learn what these machines discovered and what happened to them. The project brings forgotten explorers back into the spotlight and shows how their discoveries continue to guide science today.","details":"<p>Space Explorers: Where Are They Now? helps learners discover NASA missions through interactive stories, a map, a timeline and a quiz. We used HTML, CSS, JavaScript and NASA resources, with ChatGPT/Codex assistance. We focused on accuracy, accessibility and making space science engaging for young learners.</p>","dataRefs":[["Apollo 15 Mission\t","https://www.nasa.gov/mission/apollo-15/"],["Apollo 15 Mission Report","https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/19720021182"],["Genesis Rock","https://science.nasa.gov/solar-system/moon/genesis-rock/"],["Retracing the Steps of Apollo 15","https://science.nasa.gov/photojournal/retracing-the-steps-of-apollo-15/"],["Apollo 15 Lunar Rover Photograph","https://science.nasa.gov/resource/apollo-15-mission-image-view-of-the-apollo-lunar-surface-experiments-package-alsep/"],["Opportunity Mission","https://science.nasa.gov/mission/mer-opportunity/"],["Meridiani Planum","https://science.nasa.gov/resource/meridiani-planum-2/"],["Discovery Served Up in a Bowl","https://science.nasa.gov/resource/discovery-served-up-in-a-bowl/"],["Opportunity's Last Message","https://science.nasa.gov/resource/opportunitys-last-message/"],["Opportunity Mission Ending","https://science.nasa.gov/missions/mer/nasas-opportunity-rover-mission-on-mars-comes-to-end/"],["Opportunity Photograph: Farewell Glance at Endurance","https://science.nasa.gov/photojournal/farewell-glance-at-endurance/"],["InSight Mission Overview","https://astrobiology.nasa.gov/missions/insight/"],["InSight Science Highlights","https://science.nasa.gov/mission/insight/science-highlights/"],["InSight Mission Retirement","https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/news/nasa-retires-insight-mars-lander-mission-after-years-of-science/"],["InSight Marsquake Research","https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/news/nasas-insight-finds-marsquakes-from-meteoroids-go-deeper-than-expected/"],["InSight's Final Selfie","https://science.nasa.gov/photojournal/insights-final-selfie/"],["LCROSS Mission","https://science.nasa.gov/mission/lcross/"],["LCROSS Impact Site","https://science.nasa.gov/image-detail/20110615lcross/"],["LCROSS Image: Hits Its Mark","https://www.nasa.gov/blogs/watch-the-skies/2009/10/09/lcross-hits-its-mark/"],["Voyager 1 Mission","https://science.nasa.gov/mission/voyager/voyager-1/"],["Io Exploration","https://science.nasa.gov/jupiter/jupiter-moons/io/exploration/"],["Discovery of Active Extraterrestrial Volcanism","https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/19790052442"],["Where Are Voyager 1 and 2 Now?","https://science.nasa.gov/mission/voyager/where-are-voyager-1-and-voyager-2-now/"],["Voyager 1 Launch Photograph","https://science.nasa.gov/photojournal/voyager-1-launch-1977/"],["NASA Image and Media Guidelines","https://www.nasa.gov/nasa-brand-center/images-and-media/"]],"projectRefs":[["ChatGPT: Assistance with Research, Writing, Code and Illustrations","https://chatgpt.com/"],["OpenAI Codex: Development Assistance","https://openai.com/codex/"],["GitHub Repository","https://github.com/natalia-79/Space-explorers"],["GitHub Page","https://natalia-79.github.io/Space-explorers/#home"]],"members":[{"name":"Natalia Samaroo","country":"Trinidad and Tobago","avatar":null,"owner":true},{"name":"Keanu Samaroo","country":"Trinidad and Tobago","avatar":null,"owner":false}]}